  "body": "In the spec we are told:\n\nOpenEndedDictionary<T> is a future IDL construct. Expect it to be used as such:\n\n``` javascript\nvar meta = { \"Content-Type\": \"text/xml\", \"Breaking-Bad\": \"<3\" }\nnew Headers(meta)\n```\n\nSadly the currently linked [IDL draft](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/) does not specify what this means.  Can someone clarify how it differs from a regular dictionary?\n",
